{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537935-the-road-to-damnation","id":1537935,"title":"The Road to Damnation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-01T01:58:50-07:00","id":1537935,"title":"The Road to Damnation","content":"It's that time of year again...<br /> <br /> <img width=\"140\" height=\"181\" data-align=\"left\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/486261-thumb140.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/486261-thumb140.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/1/486261-thumb140.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_left js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <b>Faith and Power</b><br /> <br /> There is a price to immortality. As every Cainite knows, the embrace imparts with it a set of violent and predatory urges, which tempt the undead into cruelty and violence. To protect themselves from the Beast, the Children of Caine have adopted the Roads, moral codes which guide and shape their every action. Yet a Road may lead a Cainite to either salvation and damnation; and none but a fool would believe themselves truly capable of mastering the Beast within.<br /> <br /> <b>Walking the Road to Damnation</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Road to Damnation </i>is a sourcebook for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>, describing providing details on the Roads and Paths, key parts of the belief system of Cainite society. These vary from the moral codes which define the Children of Caine in the medieval period, such as the Path of Chivalry to the Path of Heaven, as well as the strangest and most unnatural faiths, including the Path of the Slain and the Path of the Scorched Heart. The book also contains details of the history of the Roads, and how they have influenced Cainite society over time, as well as guidance on incorporating various Roads and Paths into chronicles.<br /> <br /> <b>The Road to Damnation includes:</b><ul><li>An overview of the Roads, key moral codes which shape Cainite existence.</li> <li>Historical information on how the Roads developed, and guidance for their use within chronicles.</li> <li>Full information and rules for six Roads and forty-three Paths.</li> </ul><i>The Road to Damnation</i> can be found on the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486261/The-Road-to-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Vault</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T09:23:34-07:00","id":1538303,"title":"","content":"No one else has commented so I'll be the first. This looks really cool. My currently budget don't allow me to get it right away, but its on the list!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T04:41:31-07:00","id":1538940,"title":"","content":"Thank you; I have not had much time to comment on the forums recently, with other matters demanding my attention. <br /> <br /> Anyway, this is a response to the slightly lacklustre approach to Roads in DAV20; whilst they are game mechanics, they also function as a hook for rather a lot of game background, and a feature which ought to have more attention than they do. And I have been thinking about this for a while; if you go back to <i>England Will Burn</i>, published in 2019, there's some forward planning in character design to take account of what I then wanted to do in relation to Roads.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller's Vault Winter in July sale is on, so not a bad time to pick up the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=James%20Willoughby\" target=\"_blank\">back catalogue</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}